WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.283
A tall, slim girl with long red hair sat on a farmhouse doorstep one sunny afternoon in August.

2
00:00:08.284 --> 00:00:11.721
The girl's name was Anne, spelled with an "e."

3
00:00:11.722 --> 00:00:14.938
She was sixteen and a half years old.

4
00:00:14.939 --> 00:00:22.067
Anne Shirley had been living at Green Gables farm with her adoptive mother, Marilla, for the past five years.

5
00:00:22.068 --> 00:00:26.363
They had been the happiest five years of Anne's life.

6
00:00:26.364 --> 00:00:33.306
Soon Anne was going to start her first job, as a teacher at Avonlea Elementary School.

7
00:00:33.307 --> 00:00:39.373
As she sat on the doorstep, she daydreamed about her influence upon her future students.

8
00:00:39.374 --> 00:00:47.569
Anne thought some might grow up to be famous . . . a Canadian premier or an important scholar perhaps.

9
00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:54.376
It might be unlikely, Anne thought, but an excellent teacher could make all the difference.

10
00:00:54.377 --> 00:01:05.243
Anne's daydreaming was interrupted. A small cow was walking down the lane, followed by Mr. Harrison, the new neighbor.

11
00:01:05.244 --> 00:01:12.756
Without waiting to open the gate, Mr. Harrison bounded over the fence and angrily confronted Anne.

12
00:01:12.757 --> 00:01:16.486
She stood, looking at him in bewilderment.

13
00:01:16.487 --> 00:01:24.500
Mr. Harrison had only lived in Avonlea for a month, but he already had the reputation of being a little odd.

14
00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:30.314
He lived alone and had publicly stated he wanted no women around.

15
00:01:30.315 --> 00:01:36.324
The women of Avonlea, especially Mrs. Lynde, took great offense to this.

16
00:01:36.325 --> 00:01:44.594
Furthermore Mr. Harrison washed his dishes only once a week, on Sunday, and he ate his meals whenever it suited him!

17
00:01:44.595 --> 00:01:50.141
Strangest of all, Mr. Harrison owned a parrot called Ginger.

18
00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:58.148
Nobody in Avonlea had ever kept a parrot as a pet before, and apparently the parrot swore terribly.

19
00:01:58.149 --> 00:02:04.219
All these things flashed through Anne's mind as Mr. Harrison stared angrily at her.

20
00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:09.385
He was not a handsome man; he was short, fat, and bald.

21
00:02:09.386 --> 00:02:14.066
He was the ugliest person Anne had ever seen.

22
00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:18.676
"I'm not going to put up with this," Mr. Harrison shouted.

23
00:02:18.677 --> 00:02:22.667
"This is the third time, miss. The third time!"

24
00:02:22.668 --> 00:02:28.076
"Will you explain what the trouble is?" asked Anne, in her most dignified manner.

25
00:02:28.077 --> 00:02:32.585
"I found your aunt's cow in my oat field again!

26
00:02:32.586 --> 00:02:37.173
I found the cow there last Tuesday and yesterday as well!"

27
00:02:37.174 --> 00:02:44.674
"If you mean Miss Marilla Cuthbert, she is not my aunt," Anne replied, "and she is not here.

28
00:02:44.675 --> 00:02:48.299
The cow, whose name is Dolly, is mine.

29
00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:53.569
I am very sorry Dolly left her pen and wandered into your oat field."

30
00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:59.403
"You're sorry?" asked Mr. Harrison. " Sorry isn't going to

31
00:02:59.404 --> 00:03:06.533
help! Your cow has caused a lot of damage. What about my

32
00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:15.036
oats?" "I am very sorry," repeated Anne firmly, "but if you would repair your fence, Dolly wouldn't be able to get

33
00:03:15.037 --> 00:03:18.547
in." "My fence is fine," snapped Mr.

34
00:03:18.548 --> 00:03:24.457
Harrison. "A jail fence couldn't keep out that cow, you redheaded

35
00:03:24.458 --> 00:03:33.929
smarty-pants!" The color of Anne's hair had always been a tender point with her, and very soon something else besides Anne's hair became red.

36
00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:41.059
"I'd rather have red hair than no hair at all, except for a little fringe around my ears," Anne said.

37
00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:47.544
Mr. Harrison was very sensitive about his bald head, and he glared speechlessly at Anne.

38
00:03:47.545 --> 00:03:52.843
"Luckily I have an imagination," Anne continued in her best schoolteacher's voice,

39
00:03:52.844 --> 00:03:58.016
"and I can imagine it would be very annoying to have a cow in your field.

40
00:03:58.017 --> 00:04:05.417
So I will forgive you for making fun of my hair, and I promise you that Dolly will never go into your field again."

41
00:04:05.418 --> 00:04:10.379
"Well, make sure she doesn't," muttered Mr. Harrison.

42
00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:15.316
He stomped off angrily, still grumbling to himself.

43
00:04:15.317 --> 00:04:21.839
Anne turned around, marched across the yard, and put the naughty cow back into her milking pen.

44
00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.817
"She can't possibly get out now," Anne thought.

45
00:04:25.818 --> 00:04:32.264
"I should have sold her to Mr. Shearer last week, but I thought it would be better to wait for the auction.

46
00:04:32.265 --> 00:04:35.575
Well, what they say about Mr. Harrison is true.

47
00:04:35.576 --> 00:04:39.638
He is an odd and disagreeable man!"

48
00:04:39.639 --> 00:04:46.310
The next afternoon Anne and her best friend, Diana Barry, were driving home after shopping in town.

49
00:04:46.311 --> 00:04:50.814
Suddenly Anne stopped the horse and stared.

50
00:04:50.815 --> 00:04:55.062
A cow was right in the middle of Mr. Harrison's oat field!

51
00:04:55.063 --> 00:05:00.219
Anne dropped the reins, jumped down, and leaped over Mr. Harrison's fence.

52
00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:05.111
She had to get that cow before Mr. Harrison saw it!

53
00:05:05.112 --> 00:05:10.543
"Anne, come back!" Diana shrieked. "You'll ruin your dress!"

54
00:05:10.544 --> 00:05:18.871
Diana got off the buggy, tied the horse to a post, and ran into the field. "What are you doing, Anne?"

55
00:05:18.872 --> 00:05:24.551
"I must get that cow out before Mr. Harrison sees her," gasped Anne.

56
00:05:24.552 --> 00:05:28.943
"That way, Diana! Grab Dolly!" screamed Anne.

57
00:05:28.944 --> 00:05:34.414
Twenty minutes later the cow was finally back in her pen.

58
00:05:34.415 --> 00:05:41.663
As Diana and Anne trudged back to the road, they saw a buggy stopped beside Diana's buggy.

59
00:05:41.664 --> 00:05:48.931
Mr. Shearer and his son had stopped to watch in amusement as Anne and Diana chased the cow.

60
00:05:48.932 --> 00:05:54.133
Mr. Shearer chuckled and said, "You should have sold that cow to me, Anne!"

61
00:05:54.134 --> 00:06:00.379
"I'll sell her to you right now," replied Anne, flushed and disheveled.

62
00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:06.939
"All right," said Mr. Shearer. "I'll give you twenty dollars, the same as I offered before.

63
00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:10.830
My son Jim can take her into town now."

64
00:06:10.831 --> 00:06:20.984
Five minutes later Jim Shearer and the cow were marching up the road, and Anne was driving along the Green Gables lane with twenty dollars.

65
00:06:20.985 --> 00:06:24.582
"What will Marilla say?" asked Diana.

66
00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:30.381
"Oh, she won't care," said Anne. "Dolly was my cow."

67
00:06:30.382 --> 00:06:36.629
Early that evening Marilla was in the kitchen of Green Gables when she heard a shriek outside.

68
00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:40.728
Anne ran into the kitchen, looking distressed.

69
00:06:40.729 --> 00:06:44.937
"Anne Shirley, what's the matter now?" asked Marilla.

70
00:06:44.938 --> 00:06:49.365
"Oh, Marilla!" said Anne. "Whatever will I do?

71
00:06:49.366 --> 00:06:52.203
This is terrible, and it's all my fault.

72
00:06:52.204 --> 00:07:00.317
Mrs. Lynde said I would do something dreadful some day, and now I've done it!"

